              <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-5">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can I run Bifrost in mainland China?</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-700">There is no official mainland China mirror or hosted SaaS endpoint, so you cannot reach the Maxim-hosted demo from mainland without a proxy. The standard pattern is to deploy Bifrost yourself on a domestic cloud (Alibaba Cloud, Huawei Cloud, Tencent Cloud) and route only to a self-hosted upstream such as Ollama or vLLM running Qwen, GLM, or DeepSeek weights inside China. That keeps every prompt byte on-shore, satisfies data-residency requirements, and still gives you the same unified OpenAI-compatible interface as global developers. Bifrost's gateway overhead is sub-100 microseconds regardless of region.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-5">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How many providers and models does Bifrost support?</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-700">Bifrost's public site and docs (verified 2026-09-08) describe 23+ upstream providers and 1,000+ models accessible through the unified OpenAI-compatible API. Verified providers include OpenAI, Anthropic, AWS Bedrock, Google Vertex, Azure OpenAI, Cohere, Mistral, Groq, Cerebras, Ollama, Hugging Face, and Replicate, plus any custom self-deployed model. The provider list is the most comprehensive among open-source AI gateways and is the closest competitor to OpenRouter's hosted catalog.</p>
              </div>
